From 21382dba001eefd74faa9f6c60dd61f91f182c85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:28:29 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] [TSReader] Seek to the PES of the key frame

SeekTime took the landing position from AVContext::GetRecoveryPos(), but
AVContext::Reset() cleared payload_unit_pos after every TS packet. The demuxer
also emits a frame only after a later PES starts, so the PES where the
frame starts is not the PES of the last unit start. A seek then continued at
a later frame, often at the start of the next segment.

The elementary stream now records the stream position of each PES start
with the buffer offset of its data. SeekTime takes the position of the PES
where the data of the emitted frame starts.

The H.264 test frames are padded with trailing zero bytes: the parser reads
an SPS or PPS only with 64 bytes and a slice header only with 32 bytes, so
short access units took the PTS of a later PES.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
